diff --git a/doc/imv.5.txt b/doc/imv.5.txt
index 3f009fa..b9230a8 100644
--- a/doc/imv.5.txt
+++ b/doc/imv.5.txt
@@ -146,4 +146,16 @@ called 'less', '>' is called 'greater'.
 A complete list of keysyms can also be found on most systems with the
 'dumpkeys -l' command.
 
+Mouse buttons and the scroll wheel can be bound by name: '<MouseLeft>',
+'<MouseMiddle>', '<MouseRight>', '<MouseSide>', '<MouseExtra>',
+'<MouseForward>' and '<MouseBack>' for mouse buttons, and '<WheelUp>',
+'<WheelDown>', '<WheelLeft>' and '<WheelRight>' for scroll events, for
+example: '<MouseSide> = reset' or '<WheelDown> = next'. The angle brackets
+are required, as for multi-character key names. Modifiers apply to mouse
+events as well, in the same order as for keys: '<Ctrl+MouseLeft>',
+'<Ctrl+Shift+WheelUp>'. Button names carry the 'Mouse' prefix to avoid
+clashing with arrow keys and browser keysyms in the shared bind table. When
+no command is bound to a scroll event, the wheel keeps its default
+behaviour of zooming the image.
+
 **imv**(1)
